# Build output. Build/ is where the whole solution lands (see Directory.Build.props) - the
# assemblies, and the two config.json files you edit, which are yours and not the repository's.
Build/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/

# Visual Studio / Rider
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# NuGet
[Pp]ackages/
*.nupkg

# Runtime / local config (credentials + logs live here — never commit)
config.json
**/config.json
*.log
aobuddy.log

# OS
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Python bytecode (the tools/ webserver)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Recorded navigation data. These are one character's walked routes, rebuilt by simply playing,
# and they are not something a clone needs; nav_backups/ is kept as a worked example.
AOBuddy/nav/

# Mission wall triangles (20 MB). Regenerated from the client data by tools/AONavExtractor.
AOBuddy/GameData/Nav/*/walls.bin

# One-off data extractors. They ran once against a local copy of the client data and the OmniCell
# datafiles, wrote the profile JSON that IS committed, and are hard-wired to the paths of the
# machine that ran them. The generated data is the useful part.
tools/mp-*/

# Local working notes. These name the characters used for testing and quote sniff transcripts,
# so they stay on the machine that made them.
AOBuddy/CLAUDE.md

# Claude Code's own configuration and hooks. Local tooling, not part of the project.
.claude/
**/.claude/

# One-off data extractors. They ran once against a local copy of the client data and the OmniCell
# datafiles, wrote the profile JSON that IS committed, and are hard-wired to the paths of the
# machine that ran them. The generated data is the useful part.
tools/mp-*/

# Local working notes - handoffs, roadmaps and the dated design write-ups that went with each
# piece of work. They name test characters and local paths, and they go stale the moment the code
# they describe changes. The repository carries the code and the data it needs, not the diary.
HANDOFF-*.md
MILESTONES-*.md
CLASS-PROFILE-PLAYBOOK.md
*-design.md
*_DESIGN.md

# Wall triangles for the nav data: generated from your own client by tools/AONavExtractor (122 MB for
# every zone), not shipped. See AOBuddy/GameData/Nav/README.md.
AOBuddy/GameData/Nav/**/walls.bin

# AODB icons exported from the local AO client (Funcom art) - never committed
tools/aodb/icons/
